{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th Fib4 number iteratively, defined by fib4(0)=0, fib4(1)=0, fib4(2)=2, fib4(3)=0, and fib4(n)=fib4(n-1)+fib4(n-2)+fib4(n-3)+fib4(n-4) for n > 3. Raises ValueError for negative input.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize with the first four sequence values: fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n    a, b, c, d = 0, 0, 2, 0\n\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib4 = a + b + c + d\n        a, b, c, d = b, c, d, next_fib4\n    return d"}
